<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>The Day Before Your Interview</h2>
  
  <div class="timeline">
   <div class="timeline-item">
    <h4>Research the Company</h4>
    <p>Know their mission, products, recent news, and culture. Name specific things you admire.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="timeline-item">
    <h4>Review Your Experience</h4>
    <p>Know your resume cold. Be ready to discuss every project and internship.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="timeline-item">
    <h4>Prepare Questions</h4>
    <p>Have 3–5 genuine questions about the role, team, or company. Shows interest.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="timeline-item">
    <h4>Practice Out Loud</h4>
    <p>Do a mock interview with a friend or use mock interview tools.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="timeline-item">
    <h4>Get Good Sleep</h4>
    <p>Don't stay up late cramming. A clear head is your best asset.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="timeline-item">
    <h4>Dress Appropriately</h4>
    <p>Know the company dress code. If unsure, business casual. First impressions matter.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>During the Interview</h2>
  
  <div class="grid">
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">😊</div>
    <h3>Be Genuine</h3>
    <p>Be yourself. Interviewers can tell if you're faking it. Authenticity wins.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">👂</div>
    <h3>Listen Carefully</h3>
    <p>Answer the question asked, not the one you prepared. Take a breath before responding.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">❓</div>
    <h3>Ask Questions</h3>
    <p>Show curiosity and engagement. Don't just wait to answer; drive the conversation.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">✨</div>
    <h3>Show Energy</h3>
    <p>Be enthusiastic about the role and company. Positive energy is contagious.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>After the Interview</h2>
  
  <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:20px">Don't disappear after the interview. Follow up!</p>

  <div style="background:rgba(110,231,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(110,231,255,.2);border-radius:16px;padding:25px;margin:30px 0">
   <h4 style="margin-top:0">Within 24 Hours, Send a Thank-You Email:</h4>
   <p style="color:var(--muted)">Keep it short (3–4 sentences). Thank them, mention something specific from the conversation, reiterate your interest. Shows professionalism.</p>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

